{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791055676,"nonce":"ICXgxkw8K0yludgHwKcXKMsH6Rk=","message":"fd45433: glass and blur brushes draw. A Glass or Blur background emits a PRIM_BACKDROP record. Blinc's simple glass is saturation (luminance weights .299/.587/.114), then brightness, then tint.rgb*tint.a*0.5 added, all folded into the record's colour matrix; the blur brush mixes its tint over. The non-simple (liquid) glass is drawn as simple glass for now: no edge refraction, light highlights, noise or border_color edge band. 74545da: every blur pass (layer blur, drop shadow, backdrop) reads texel pairs through the linear sampler at the ratio of their weights, instead of skipping texels at large deviations, which aliased into a grid on heavy blurs. Left: liquid glass, evenodd clip fill (waits on Blinc).","files":null}]}